### Step 1: Understand the roots of unity

A 13th root of unity is a complex number $ \omega $ such that:

$$
\omega^{13} = 1, \quad \omega \neq 1
$$

So the 13th roots of unity are:

$$
\omega, \omega^2, \omega^3, \ldots, \omega^{12}
$$

These are all the complex numbers that satisfy $ x^{13} = 1 $, and they form a group under multiplication (the multiplicative group of the 13th roots of unity).

